    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the high-upside matchup against Lowder, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** and **Gabriel Moreno**. **Corbin Carroll** earns our highest daily efficiency score at 85.93, benefiting from a massive +19% boost due to the favorable SP_xERA and a high-leverage #2 spot in the order that maximizes his stolen base potential. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.83) is a locked-in start against Burrows, where a +14% platoon edge and the standard order advantage provide a robust floor. **James Wood** (65.46) also projects as a strong start; despite a tougher draw against Castillo, his elite 0.403 xwOBA and top-of-the-order positioning make him an essential asset in our 5x5 framework.\n\nWe are navigating several risks with \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Max Muncy**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Seiya Suzuki**. While **Max Muncy** (59.63) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.44) remain startable, **Seiya Suzuki** (44.52) sits precariously close to the sub-40 floor due to a poor matchup against McDonald and limited defensive metrics. The most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (44.90); he narrowly missed the cut because the combination of a difficult southpaw in Manaea and a -14% SP skill handicap suppressed his utility relative to our other infield options. Meanwhile, **Travis Bazzana** was never in consideration, as his sub-40 score against an elite arm like Skubal confirms he should remain sidelined to preserve our season-long game caps. We are also monitoring **Brice Turang** (54.44) and **Cole Young** (47.78) closely; while both are essential for speed, they face high-k efficiency from their respective opponents, requiring them to stay aggressive on the basepaths to justify their inclusion over safer bench alternatives like **Alex Freeland**.",
